      "body": "## Overview\n\nExplain how execution settings can change greedy output. Add guidance to compare logprobs at the same input prefix and check the gap between the two leading tokens.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Separate repeatability within one configuration from agreement across configurations.\n- Explain how numerical rounding can change the selected token at a near tie.\n- Make clear that a small token gap alone does not rule out a kernel bug.\n\n## Validation\n\nThis change only updates documentation. It does not change model execution or sampling.\n\n```bash\npre-commit run --files docs/features/batch_invariance.md\n```\n\nAll applicable hooks passed on the updated branch, including spelling and Markdown lint. The execution flags were checked against the current source and compile debugging guide. No new model benchmark was run. Upstream test CI is blocked by the contributor gate.\n\n## Details\n\nChanging compilation or CUDA graph settings can change kernel selection and rounding. The size of a logprob difference depends on the model, prompt, hardware, and settings. The text avoids a universal numerical range and a universal default execution mode.\n\nOpen PR searches found no other documentation change for this cross-mode comparison. [#55238](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/55238) records the related investigation. Related batch-invariance kernel PRs change execution behavior.\n\nAI assistance was used.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull Request Checklist</summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
